    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as our undisputed anchor. With a score of 83.69, his favorable matchup against J. Lopez (5.06 xERA) combined with an optimal #3 spot in the order makes him our highest-upside play. **Yordan Alvarez** follows closely at 73.20; despite a slight park penalty, his elite 0.467 xwOBA remains the most potent weapon in our arsenal against Tidwell. We are leaning into significant platoon advantages today, most notably with **Caleb Durbin** (62.57) and **Lars Nootbaar** (56.75), both of whom benefit from dynamic platoon splits against their respective right-handed opponents to push them into viable starting territory despite middling SP xERAs.\n\nOur bench situation is relatively straightforward today as **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith** are all unavailable due to off-days or rest. Consequently, our depth pieces like **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** are effectively sidelined. **Kyle Schwarber** narrowly makes the cut as our UTIL option (59.99); his high-leverage leadoff spot provides enough plate-appearance value to justify the start despite a slightly unfavorable park factor. \n\nWe are monitoring the bottom of our lineup closely, as **Josh Smith** (51.05) and **Christian Yelich** (57.13) hover near the marginal threshold. **Josh Smith** is hindered by an #8 batting order slot, though his platoon edge against Gray prevents him from falling into the \"below floor\" category. Owners should remain vigilant regarding weather risks; while no specific rainouts are projected for these venues, the reliance on mid-tier SP xERAs across the board suggests a high-variance day where we are prioritizing pure volume and platoon optimization to preserve our remaining games cap.",
